{"book":13,"chapter":40,"rubric":"PYTHON AS A FIRST LANGUAGE / CLASS DESIGN / CHAPTER 40","slides":[{"title":"Contract","sub":"Why abstract classes","short":"Contract","main":"An abstract class is a promise that every subclass keeps.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Duck typing","Growing pains","Contract"],"captions":["Quacks, so it is a duck: enough for small programs","Which methods must an object have? What if a developer forgets one? Find out before running, not after release?","An abstract class is a contract: a promise every subclass must keep"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":70.0,"w":110.0,"h":34.0,"text":"quacks?","tone":"blue","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":70.0,"w":110.0,"h":34.0,"text":"so a duck","tone":"green","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":146.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":214.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6}],[{"t":"text","id":"q1","x":180.0,"y":40.0,"text":"which methods?","size":11.0},{"t":"text","id":"q2","x":180.0,"y":76.0,"text":"what if one is missing?","size":11.0},{"t":"text","id":"q3","x":180.0,"y":112.0,"text":"know before release?","tone":"yellow","size":11.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":180.0,"y":36.0,"w":140.0,"h":28.0,"text":"contract","tone":"yellow","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":110.0,"w":100.0,"h":26.0,"text":"Subclass 1","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":110.0,"w":100.0,"h":26.0,"text":"Subclass 2","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":150.0,"y1":50.0,"x2":106.0,"y2":96.0,"tone":"yellow","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":210.0,"y1":50.0,"x2":254.0,"y2":96.0,"tone":"yellow","arrow":true,"width":1.6}]],"cues":[15.9,30.3]}]},{"title":"ABC and abstractmethod","sub":"Cannot instantiate without implementation","short":"ABC","main":"A forgotten method shows up when the object is created.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Declaration","Cannot instantiate","Subclass"],"captions":["Inherit from ABC and mark required methods with @abstractmethod","Instantiation fails: TypeError lists the unimplemented methods","A subclass that implements everything works; a forgotten method is caught at creation"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":24.0,"y":44.0,"lines":["from abc import ABC, abstractmethod","","class Shape(ABC):","    @abstractmethod","    def area(self): ..."],"hl":[3,4],"lang":"python","size":10.5,"lh":22.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":56.0,"lines":["Shape()","# TypeError: Can't instantiate abstract","# class Shape without an implementation","# for abstract method 'area'"],"bad":[0,1,2,3],"lang":"python","size":10.5,"lh":24.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":56.0,"lines":["class Rect(Shape):","    def __init__(self, w, h): ...","    def area(self):","        return self.w * self.h","Rect(2, 3).area()   # 6"],"hl":[2,3],"lang":"python","size":10.5,"lh":22.0,"w":320.0}]],"cues":[14.1,22.6]}]},{"title":"How it works","sub":"ABCMeta","short":"ABCMeta","main":"Without ABC the decorator is silently ignored.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["ABCMeta","Check","Without ABC"],"captions":["ABC has the ABCMeta metaclass: on class creation it collects abstract method names into __abstractmethods__","Checked at instantiation: set not empty - creation rejected","Forgot to inherit from ABC - decorator silently ignored; check abstractness with a test"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":70.0,"w":110.0,"h":30.0,"text":"ABCMeta","tone":"yellow","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":70.0,"w":150.0,"h":30.0,"text":"__abstractmethods__","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":146.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":192.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":56.0,"lines":["Shape.__abstractmethods__","# frozenset({'area'})","Rect.__abstractmethods__","# frozenset()"],"hl":[0,1],"lang":"python","size":11.0,"lh":24.0,"w":300.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":56.0,"lines":["class Shape:            # no ABC!","    @abstractmethod","    def area(self): ...","Shape()    # created: no check"],"bad":[0,3],"lang":"python","size":10.5,"lh":24.0,"w":320.0}]],"cues":[14.7,31.9]}]},{"title":"Body and properties","sub":"Abstract property and classmethod","short":"Properties","main":"@property or @classmethod on top, @abstractmethod below.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Abstract with a body","Property","Order"],"captions":["An abstract method may have a body: a subclass calls it via super() and extends it","Properties and factories can be abstract too: @property or @classmethod on top, @abstractmethod below","Then subclasses must define both the property and the factory - the whole contract"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":24.0,"y":44.0,"lines":["@abstractmethod","def describe(self):","    return 'shared part'","# subclass:","def describe(self):","    return super().describe() + '+own'"],"hl":[2,5],"lang":"python","size":10.0,"lh":20.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":24.0,"y":44.0,"lines":["@property","@abstractmethod","def name(self): ...","","@classmethod","@abstractmethod","def create(cls): ..."],"hl":[0,1,4,5],"lang":"python","size":10.0,"lh":18.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":56.0,"w":110.0,"h":28.0,"text":"@property","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":90.0,"y":100.0,"w":130.0,"h":28.0,"text":"@abstractmethod","tone":"yellow","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c~cell","x":270.0,"y":78.0,"w":90.0,"h":28.0,"text":"def name","tone":"blue","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":90.0,"y1":72.0,"x2":90.0,"y2":86.0,"tone":"muted","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":156.0,"y1":100.0,"x2":226.0,"y2":82.0,"tone":"muted","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":270.0,"y":118.0,"text":"top → bottom","size":10.0}]],"cues":[11.2,23.9]}]},{"title":"Template method","sub":"An algorithm of steps","short":"Template method","main":"Call order in the base class, steps in subclasses.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["An algorithm of steps","Own step","Order is fixed"],"captions":["The base class holds a ready algorithm: header, body, footer","Header and footer are shared, the body is an abstract step: each report has its own","A subclass writes only the missing steps, call order stays the same - this is how framework lifecycles work"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":70.0,"y":70.0,"w":90.0,"h":30.0,"text":"header()","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":180.0,"y":70.0,"w":90.0,"h":30.0,"text":"body()","tone":"yellow","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":290.0,"y":70.0,"w":90.0,"h":30.0,"text":"footer()","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":116.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":134.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"muted","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":226.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":244.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"muted","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":118.0,"text":"render()","size":11.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c~code","x":24.0,"y":44.0,"lines":["class Report(ABC):","    def render(self):","        return self.header() + self.body() + self.footer()","    @abstractmethod","    def body(self): ..."],"hl":[2,3,4],"lang":"python","size":9.5,"lh":22.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c~code","x":24.0,"y":56.0,"lines":["class Sales(Report):","    def body(self):","        return 'sales: 42'","Sales().render()"],"hl":[1,2,3],"lang":"python","size":11.0,"lh":24.0,"w":320.0}]],"cues":[10.5,25.2]}]},{"title":"Virtual subclasses","sub":"register and __subclasshook__","short":"register","main":"An object with the right method is already Sized.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["register","__subclasshook__","Sized"],"captions":["ABC.register(Cls) declares a subclass without inheritance - isinstance confirms it","__subclasshook__ sets the condition automatically: any class with the right method counts as a subclass","This is how Sized and Iterable work: an object with __len__ is Sized without inheriting from anything"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":56.0,"lines":["Quacker.register(Duck)","isinstance(Duck(), Quacker)   # True","issubclass(Duck, Quacker)   # True"],"hl":[0],"lang":"python","size":11.0,"lh":26.0,"w":310.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":24.0,"y":44.0,"lines":["class HasLen(ABC):","    @classmethod","    def __subclasshook__(cls, C):","        if cls is HasLen:","            return hasattr(C, '__len__')","        return NotImplemented"],"hl":[4],"lang":"python","size":10.0,"lh":20.0,"w":330.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":70.0,"w":110.0,"h":30.0,"text":"class Box:\n__len__","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":70.0,"w":100.0,"h":30.0,"text":"Sized","tone":"green","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":146.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":218.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"dash":"3 3","width":1.6},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":118.0,"text":"isinstance(Box(), Sized) → True","size":10.0}]],"cues":[13.9,27.9]}]},{"title":"collections.abc","sub":"Ready-made contracts","short":"collections.abc","main":"Two methods - and a dozen ready ones.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Ready-made contracts","Sequence","Checks"],"captions":["collections.abc has Sequence, Mapping, Set, Iterable, Iterator, Callable and more","Sequence needs __len__ and __getitem__; iteration, in, count, index, reversed come for free","isinstance(x, Iterable) accepts any iterable, not just a list"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"b0","x":62.0,"y":54.0,"w":104.0,"h":26.0,"text":"Sequence","tone":"green","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b1","x":180.0,"y":54.0,"w":104.0,"h":26.0,"text":"Mapping","tone":"green","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b2","x":298.0,"y":54.0,"w":104.0,"h":26.0,"text":"Set","tone":"green","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b3","x":62.0,"y":94.0,"w":104.0,"h":26.0,"text":"Iterable","tone":"green","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b4","x":180.0,"y":94.0,"w":104.0,"h":26.0,"text":"Iterator","tone":"green","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b5","x":298.0,"y":94.0,"w":104.0,"h":26.0,"text":"Callable","tone":"green","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":44.0,"w":130.0,"h":24.0,"text":"__len__","tone":"green","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":90.0,"y":78.0,"w":130.0,"h":24.0,"text":"__getitem__","tone":"green","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"m0","x":260.0,"y":30.0,"w":104.0,"h":22.0,"text":"__iter__","tone":"yellow","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"m1","x":260.0,"y":58.0,"w":104.0,"h":22.0,"text":"__contains__","tone":"yellow","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"m2","x":260.0,"y":86.0,"w":104.0,"h":22.0,"text":"count","tone":"yellow","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"m3","x":260.0,"y":114.0,"w":104.0,"h":22.0,"text":"index","tone":"yellow","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"m4","x":260.0,"y":142.0,"w":104.0,"h":22.0,"text":"__reversed__","tone":"yellow","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":56.0,"lines":["isinstance([], Iterable)       # True","isinstance({}, Iterable)       # True","isinstance(5, Iterable)        # False"],"lang":"python","size":10.5,"lh":26.0,"w":320.0}]],"cues":[12.4,29.8]}]},{"title":"Numeric tower","sub":"numbers","short":"numbers","main":"Check against abstract classes, not int.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Numeric tower","Integral","Generality"],"captions":["Number ⊃ Complex ⊃ Real ⊃ Rational ⊃ Integral: each one narrower than the last","isinstance(x, Integral) accepts integers of any kind - int, bool, third-party numbers","Check generic functions against abstract classes, but often it is better to just try the operation"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":180.0,"y":24.0,"w":220.0,"h":22.0,"text":"Number","tone":"muted","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n1","x":180.0,"y":54.0,"w":184.0,"h":22.0,"text":"Complex","tone":"blue","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n2","x":180.0,"y":84.0,"w":148.0,"h":22.0,"text":"Real","tone":"green","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n3","x":180.0,"y":114.0,"w":112.0,"h":22.0,"text":"Rational","tone":"yellow","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n4","x":180.0,"y":144.0,"w":76.0,"h":22.0,"text":"Integral","tone":"violet","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":40.0,"y":56.0,"lines":["isinstance(True, Integral)    # True","isinstance(3.5, Integral)    # False","isinstance(Fraction(1,2), Rational)"],"lang":"python","size":10.5,"lh":26.0,"w":310.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":70.0,"w":110.0,"h":30.0,"text":"Number","tone":"green","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":70.0,"w":110.0,"h":30.0,"text":"your type too","tone":"blue","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":118.0,"text":"foreign types fit too","size":10.0}]],"cues":[10.6,21.9]}]},{"title":"Substitution principle","sub":"Liskov","short":"Substitution","main":"Do not require more, do not promise less.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Substitution","Do not require more","Do not promise less"],"captions":["A subclass must fit wherever the base class is expected (Liskov principle)","Base accepts any number, subclass rejects negatives - the program breaks unexpectedly","Base returns a list, subclass returns None: a contract is meaning, not just names; write it in the docs"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":70.0,"w":110.0,"h":30.0,"text":"Base","tone":"blue","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":70.0,"w":110.0,"h":30.0,"text":"Child","tone":"green","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":216.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":146.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":118.0,"text":"wherever Base is expected","size":10.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":28.0,"text":"Base: any number","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":28.0,"text":"Child: x ≥ 0 ✗","tone":"red","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":112.0,"text":"cannot tighten input","tone":"red","size":10.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":28.0,"text":"Base → list","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":28.0,"text":"Child → None ✗","tone":"red","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":112.0,"text":"cannot weaken output","tone":"red","size":10.0}]],"cues":[15.4,29.4]}]},{"title":"Storages","sub":"Dependency injection","short":"Storages","main":"The app knows the interface, not the implementation.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Interface","Implementations","Swap in tests"],"captions":["Storage defines what any storage can do: read and write","Implementations: in memory, on disk, in the cloud - all keep the contract","The app takes Storage and does not know the implementation; tests plug in a simple stand-in (dependency injection)"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"s","x":180.0,"y":50.0,"w":160.0,"h":34.0,"text":"Storage (ABC)","tone":"yellow","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"r","x":110.0,"y":110.0,"w":90.0,"h":22.0,"text":"read()","tone":"green","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"w","x":250.0,"y":110.0,"w":90.0,"h":22.0,"text":"write()","tone":"green","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"s","x":180.0,"y":34.0,"w":140.0,"h":26.0,"text":"Storage","tone":"yellow","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"i0","x":70.0,"y":112.0,"w":84.0,"h":26.0,"text":"Memory","tone":"green","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"i1","x":180.0,"y":112.0,"w":84.0,"h":26.0,"text":"Disk","tone":"green","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"i2","x":290.0,"y":112.0,"w":84.0,"h":26.0,"text":"Cloud","tone":"gr